{The parent gives H0 and H1 equal weight in every state. The main modification is to increase H0's weight smoothly with relative dispersion in unfinished-job remaining work, hypothesizing that H0's positive remaining-work term deserves more emphasis when job workloads are uneven, whereas H1 penalizes estimated tail work. Equal weighting remains the baseline when remaining workloads are identical; this hypothesis requires complete-schedule evaluation.}
```python
def use_heuristics(progress, candidate_pair_ratio, remaining_work_mean, remaining_work_std, machine_ready_mean, machine_ready_std, previous_heuristic):
    dispersion = remaining_work_std / (remaining_work_mean + remaining_work_std)
    alpha = 0.5 + 0.3 * dispersion
    return (1, (alpha, 1.0 - alpha, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0))
```
